==================================================================
DAY 38 - PART B: LAB
Prepare 3 VMs for kubeadm
Time: 90-120 minutes
==================================================================

Below, commands marked [ALL] run on cp1, worker1 and worker2.
Pick ONE of the OS sections (RHEL/Rocky or Ubuntu).
Set the version once (use the version you want to START from; Day 40
upgrades one minor version up):
  K8S=v1.33


STEP 1: Create the VMs
----------------------
Example with Multipass (Ubuntu):
  multipass launch 24.04 --name cp1     --cpus 2 --memory 3G --disk 20G
  multipass launch 24.04 --name worker1 --cpus 2 --memory 2G --disk 20G
  multipass launch 24.04 --name worker2 --cpus 2 --memory 2G --disk 20G
  multipass list
  multipass shell cp1
Or create 3 Rocky 9 VMs in VirtualBox/KVM with a bridged or host-only
+ NAT network. Note their IPs.


STEP 2: Hostnames and /etc/hosts [ALL]
--------------------------------------
sudo hostnamectl set-hostname cp1        # worker1 / worker2 on the others
cat <<EOF | sudo tee -a /etc/hosts
<IP-cp1>      cp1
<IP-worker1>  worker1
<IP-worker2>  worker2
EOF
ping -c1 worker1 ; ping -c1 cp1
sudo cat /sys/class/dmi/id/product_uuid     # must differ per VM


STEP 3: Swap off [ALL]
----------------------
sudo swapoff -a
sudo sed -i '/\sswap\s/ s/^/#/' /etc/fstab
free -h            # Swap: 0B
(Ubuntu with zram/swapfile: also "sudo systemctl mask swap.target"
 or remove /swap.img entry.)


STEP 4: Kernel modules and sysctls [ALL]
----------------------------------------
cat <<EOF | sudo tee /etc/modules-load.d/k8s.conf
overlay
br_netfilter
EOF
sudo modprobe overlay
sudo modprobe br_netfilter

cat <<EOF | sudo tee /etc/sysctl.d/k8s.conf
net.bridge.bridge-nf-call-iptables  = 1
net.bridge.bridge-nf-call-ip6tables = 1
net.ipv4.ip_forward                 = 1
EOF
sudo sysctl --system
lsmod | grep -E "overlay|br_netfilter"
sysctl net.ipv4.ip_forward net.bridge.bridge-nf-call-iptables


STEP 5 (RHEL/Rocky only): SELinux and firewall [ALL]
----------------------------------------------------
sudo setenforce 0
sudo sed -i 's/^SELINUX=enforcing/SELINUX=permissive/' /etc/selinux/config
For a lab, simplest:
  sudo systemctl disable --now firewalld
Or open ports (control plane example):
  sudo firewall-cmd --permanent --add-port={6443,2379-2380,10250,10257,10259,179,4789,5473}/tcp
  sudo firewall-cmd --permanent --add-port=4789/udp
  sudo firewall-cmd --reload
  (workers: 10250, 30000-32767/tcp, 179, 4789/udp, 5473)


STEP 6: Install containerd [ALL]
--------------------------------
Ubuntu:
  sudo apt-get update
  sudo apt-get install -y containerd

RHEL/Rocky (containerd.io from Docker's repo):
  sudo dnf install -y dnf-plugins-core
  sudo dnf config-manager --add-repo https://download.docker.com/linux/rhel/docker-ce.repo
  sudo dnf install -y containerd.io

Configure systemd cgroups:
  sudo mkdir -p /etc/containerd
  containerd config default | sudo tee /etc/containerd/config.toml >/dev/null
  sudo sed -i 's/SystemdCgroup = false/SystemdCgroup = true/' /etc/containerd/config.toml
  grep -n SystemdCgroup /etc/containerd/config.toml     # must show true
  sudo systemctl enable --now containerd
  sudo systemctl restart containerd
  systemctl status containerd --no-pager | head -5

If grep shows nothing, your containerd version uses a different
layout; find the runc options section in config.toml and add
"SystemdCgroup = true" under it (see containerd docs for your version).
Also make sure the "cri" plugin is NOT listed in disabled_plugins.


STEP 7: Install kubeadm, kubelet, kubectl [ALL]
-----------------------------------------------
Ubuntu:
  sudo apt-get install -y apt-transport-https ca-certificates curl gpg
  sudo mkdir -p -m 755 /etc/apt/keyrings
  curl -fsSL https://pkgs.k8s.io/core:/stable:/$K8S/deb/Release.key | sudo gpg --dearmor -o /etc/apt/keyrings/kubernetes-apt-keyring.gpg
  echo "deb [signed-by=/etc/apt/keyrings/kubernetes-apt-keyring.gpg] https://pkgs.k8s.io/core:/stable:/$K8S/deb/ /" | sudo tee /etc/apt/sources.list.d/kubernetes.list
  sudo apt-get update
  sudo apt-get install -y kubelet kubeadm kubectl
  sudo apt-mark hold kubelet kubeadm kubectl

RHEL/Rocky:
  cat <<EOF | sudo tee /etc/yum.repos.d/kubernetes.repo
[kubernetes]
name=Kubernetes
baseurl=https://pkgs.k8s.io/core:/stable:/$K8S/rpm/
enabled=1
gpgcheck=1
gpgkey=https://pkgs.k8s.io/core:/stable:/$K8S/rpm/repodata/repomd.xml.key
exclude=kubelet kubeadm kubectl cri-tools kubernetes-cni
EOF
  sudo dnf install -y kubelet kubeadm kubectl --disableexcludes=kubernetes

Both:
  sudo systemctl enable --now kubelet
  kubeadm version ; kubelet --version ; kubectl version --client

The kubelet will restart every few seconds until kubeadm init/join:
that's expected.
  systemctl status kubelet --no-pager | head -5


STEP 8: crictl config [ALL]
---------------------------
cat <<EOF | sudo tee /etc/crictl.yaml
runtime-endpoint: unix:///run/containerd/containerd.sock
image-endpoint: unix:///run/containerd/containerd.sock
EOF
sudo crictl info | head -20
sudo crictl images


STEP 9: Pre-flight check
------------------------
On cp1:
  sudo kubeadm config images pull
  sudo crictl images              # apiserver, etcd, scheduler ...
  sudo kubeadm init phase preflight

Fix every [ERROR] before tomorrow. Note any [WARNING].


